        {
          "kind": "howto",
          "title": "How to drive under cab signals, ACSES, PTC, ATS and the alerter",
          "cols": 3,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "title": "Cab signal downgrade (ATC)",
              "steps": [
                "The cab display drops (e.g. Clear to Approach) and the alarm sounds.",
                "Within about 6 s: **Acknowledge** (see the card for your train) and put the automatic brake in **Suppression** (EMUs: controller to Coast and brake).",
                "Release once below the new cab-signal speed.",
                "Some trains (LIRR) want every cab-speed change acknowledged, upgrades too."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "ACSES speed and stop enforcement",
              "steps": [
                "Watch the ACSES target speed and distance on the display.",
                "When the warning sounds, acknowledge and brake to the target before the restriction.",
                "Positive stop: ACSES stops you within 1000 ft of an absolute signal at Stop. With permission press Stop Release (in the cab), then max 15 mph through the interlocking."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "PTC in TSW",
              "bullets": [
                "Keep the PTC fuse in where the train has one; the display may light, but TSW does not enforce PTC.",
                "Drive to the wayside signals and the speed signs yourself.",
                "Real I-ETMS counts down to an enforcement; brake and the warning clears."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "ATS (Metrolink, Tri-Rail Rotem)",
              "steps": [
                "Passing an inductor at any signal but Clear the ATS alarm sounds.",
                "Press **ATS acknowledge** within about 8 s: ENG 2 on the Rotem cab cars, in the cab on the F125, F59PHR and MP36.",
                "Then drive to the signal aspect."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Alerter",
              "steps": [
                "Keep the alerter cut in (aux square, fuse in).",
                "When the alerter light flashes or the buzzer sounds, reset it with the **gear lever** (or move a control).",
                "Missed: penalty brake. Stop, brake handle to Suppression, reset, then release."
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Penalty brake recovery",
              "steps": [
                "Throttle to Idle, automatic brake handle to **Suppression** (or Full Service).",
                "Wait until the PCS lamp goes out (a minute or so).",
                "Release the brake, recharge, then continue."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "title": "Before departure:",
          "text": "Alerter, ATC / ACSES (or PTC, ATS) cut in: fuses in, cut-out squares as the train's manual says. Cab signal and wayside signal agree. Check in the train's manual which control acknowledges the cab signal: gear lever, ENG 2 or the cab."
        }
      ]
